L0011: Diagnostic count limit exceeded

The compiler encountered more diagnostics than its deterministic reporting limit. The final retained diagnostic reports the ceiling. Fix the earlier root errors and run again; suppressing extra messages does not turn a rejected program into an accepted one.

Driver/resource example; generated-input tests cover this case.

```text
# Repeated lexical errors exceed the diagnostic budget.
python3 -c 'print("` " * 1001)' > many-errors.lc
locus check many-errors.lc
```

Language, as built: [1.21:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.21:1).
